{% doc %}
  Renders a section setting value, or falls back to a locale-file translation
  when (a) the viewer's locale is not English AND (b) the setting still equals
  the English default (i.e. the merchant hasn't customized it).

  Once the merchant customizes the field or sets up Shopify's Translate & Adapt,
  `value` will already contain the correct per-locale text and is used as-is.

  @param {string} value - the current section/block setting value
  @param {string} key - the locale key to look up (e.g. "homepage.hero.heading")
  @param {string} default - the English default string used to detect non-customization

  @example
  {% render 'i18n-default', value: section.settings.heading, key: 'homepage.hero.heading', default: 'Handmade coastal pieces for warm, lived-in beach homes.' %}
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign output = value
  if request.locale.iso_code != 'en' and value == default
    capture translated
      echo key | t
    endcapture
    unless translated contains 'translation missing'
      assign output = translated
    endunless
  endif
  echo output
-%}
